{
  "id": "differential-calculus",
  "title": "Differential Calculus",
  "term": 2,
  "summary": "Limits, the derivative from first principles, rules of differentiation, equations of tangents, sketching cubic graphs, concavity, and optimisation and rate-of-change problems.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The derivative"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The **derivative** $f'(x)$ gives the **gradient of the tangent** to the curve at any point, i.e. the instantaneous rate of change. It is defined as a limit of average gradients:"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "latex": "f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(x + h) - f(x)}{h}",
      "caption": "The derivative from first principles"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 1: first principles",
      "problem": "Find $f'(x)$ from first principles if $f(x) = 2x^2$.",
      "steps": [
        "$f(x + h) = 2(x + h)^2 = 2x^2 + 4xh + 2h^2$",
        "$\\dfrac{f(x + h) - f(x)}{h} = \\dfrac{4xh + 2h^2}{h} = 4x + 2h$",
        "$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(4x + 2h) = 4x$"
      ],
      "answer": "$f'(x) = 4x$"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Rules of differentiation"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Rule",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(k) = 0$",
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(7) = 0$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n) = nx^{n-1}$",
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^5) = 5x^4$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(kx^n) = knx^{n-1}$",
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x^4) = 12x^3$"
        ],
        [
          "Differentiate term by term",
          "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^3 - 2x) = 3x^2 - 2$"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 2",
      "problem": "Find $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ if $y = \\dfrac{x^3 - 4x}{x} + \\dfrac{2}{x^2}$.",
      "steps": [
        "Simplify first: $y = x^2 - 4 + 2x^{-2}$",
        "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 4x^{-3} = 2x - \\dfrac{4}{x^3}$"
      ],
      "answer": "$2x - \\frac{4}{x^3}$"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Equation of a tangent"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 3",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent to $f(x) = x^3 - 3x$ at $x = 2$.",
      "steps": [
        "$f(2) = 2$, so the point is $(2; 2)$.",
        "$f'(x) = 3x^2 - 3$, so $m = f'(2) = 9$.",
        "$y - 2 = 9(x - 2)$, so $y = 9x - 16$."
      ],
      "answer": "$y = 9x - 16$"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Sketching cubic graphs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        "$y$-intercept: let $x = 0$.",
        "$x$-intercepts: solve $f(x) = 0$ (factor theorem).",
        "Stationary points: solve $f'(x) = 0$; find the $y$-values.",
        "Point of inflection: solve $f''(x) = 0$ (concavity changes here).",
        "Shape: $a > 0$ rises to the right; $a < 0$ falls to the right."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 4",
      "problem": "Sketch $f(x) = x^3 - 3x^2$.",
      "steps": [
        "$y$-intercept $(0; 0)$; $x$-intercepts: $x^2(x - 3) = 0$ gives $(0; 0)$ and $(3; 0)$.",
        "$f'(x) = 3x^2 - 6x = 3x(x - 2) = 0$: stationary points $(0; 0)$ (local maximum) and $(2; -4)$ (local minimum).",
        "$f''(x) = 6x - 6 = 0$: point of inflection at $(1; -2)$."
      ],
      "answer": "See the graph"
    },
